---
title: Shredded Potato with Green Pepper (Qing Jiao Tu Dou Si 青椒土豆丝)
description: A homestyle Chinese comfort dish. Thinly julienned potatoes are stir-fried until crisp-tender and tangy, paired with fresh green peppers.
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 5 minutes
servings: 2
tags:
  - potato
  - bell pepper
  - vegetable
  - chinese
  - side
cuisine: Chinese
course: Side
---

> The secret to this dish is soaking the shredded potatoes to remove starch. This ensures they cook up crisp and separate, rather than mushy and stuck together.

== Prepare Potatoes ==

Peel the @waxy potatoes{2%medium} (like Yukon Gold). Julienne them into very thin matchsticks, as evenly as possible.

Place the shredded potatoes in a large #bowl{} of cold water. Swish them around to wash off the starch, then drain. Refill with fresh cold water and let them soak for ~{10%minutes}. Drain thoroughly before cooking.

== Prepare Other Ingredients ==

Core and julienne the @green bell pepper{1%medium}.
Slice the @garlic{2%cloves}.
Slice the @scallion{1%stalk}.

== Stir-fry ==

Heat a #wok{} over high heat. Add @neutral oil{2%tbsp}. Add the sliced garlic, scallion, and @dried chilies{2%whole} (optional) and fry for ~{10%seconds} until fragrant.

Add the drained shredded potatoes. Stir-fry constantly for ~{2%minutes} until they start to turn translucent.

== Season and Finish ==

Add the shredded green pepper to the wok.

Quickly season with:
- @white vinegar{1.5%tbsp} (add this down the side of the wok)
- @salt{½%tsp}
- @sugar{¼%tsp}

Toss rapidly for another ~{1%minute}. The potatoes should be cooked through but still have a slight crunch. Do not overcook.

Drizzle with @toasted sesame oil{½%tsp}, give a final toss, and serve.